stylepersonal-column-functions = Columns
stylepersonal-column-functions-introduce = Columns created or modified by Refolio for Zotero. You need to enable them manually. In the Zotero main interface, click View in the Zotero top bar, then Columns, and check the ones you want to display. Each column has corresponding settings. You can right-click any column name in the main interface to access the column settings for further customization.
stylepersonal-tab-step-columns-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-columns-2 = View › Columns
stylepersonal-tab-step-columns-3 = Right-click header
stylepersonal-tab-step-viewmgr-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-viewmgr-2 = Save view
stylepersonal-tab-step-viewmgr-3 = Switch via right-click
stylepersonal-tab-step-reader-1 = Enable features
stylepersonal-tab-step-reader-2 = Open PDF
stylepersonal-tab-step-sidepanel-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-sidepanel-2 = Set shortcut
stylepersonal-tab-step-sidepanel-3 = Quick toggle
stylepersonal-tab-step-tags-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-tags-2 = Set shortcut
stylepersonal-tab-step-tags-3 = Quick tag
stylepersonal-tab-step-collections-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-collections-2 = Organize
stylepersonal-tab-step-menu-1 = Enable
stylepersonal-tab-step-menu-2 = Right-click item
stylepersonal-tab-step-storage-1 = Choose storage
stylepersonal-tab-step-storage-2 = Auto-record progress
stylepersonal-tab-info-columns-title = Custom Item Columns
stylepersonal-tab-info-columns-desc = Refolio adds or enhances item list columns. Enable via View › Columns in the main toolbar; right-click any column header to configure further.

stylepersonal-view-manager-function = Views
stylepersonal-view-manager-function-introduce = As the number of columns increases, you may frequently need to show/hide certain columns for different use cases. View groups allow you to store and quickly switch between the current column states.
stylepersonal-tab-info-viewmgr-title = View Groups · Quick Layout Switching
stylepersonal-tab-info-viewmgr-desc = Save current column states as view groups and switch between them instantly to handle different workflows with ease.

stylepersonal-collection-functions = Collections
stylepersonal-collection-functions-introduce = Refolio adds many useful functions to the collection panel, such as sorting collections, pinning collections, and showing the number of items under each collection.
stylepersonal-tab-info-collections-title = Collection Panel Enhancement
stylepersonal-tab-info-collections-desc = Shows item counts per collection, supports sorting and pinning favorites for fast navigation to frequently used collections.

stylepersonal-tags-functions = Tags
stylepersonal-tags-functions-introduce = Tags, #Tags, nested tags—how do you quickly create and better display these tags? Learn about the following functions.
stylepersonal-tab-info-tags-title = Tag Management & Quick Entry
stylepersonal-tab-info-tags-desc = Use shortcuts to quickly add tags; nested tags provide hierarchy; #tags appear directly in the title column for at-a-glance recognition.

stylepersonal-sidepanel-functions = Sidebar
stylepersonal-sidepanel-functions-introduce = In the main interface, the entry information panel can be referred to as the right sidebar, while the collection panel can be called the left sidebar. When opening a PDF, the left sidebar changes to show annotations and outlines, while the right sidebar remains as the entry information panel.
stylepersonal-tab-info-sidepanel-title = Sidebar Quick Actions
stylepersonal-tab-info-sidepanel-desc = Right sidebar shows item info; left sidebar shows collections. Set shortcuts to quickly toggle them. Supports TLDR auto-translation.

stylepersonal-item-menu-functions = Context Menu
stylepersonal-item-menu-functions-introduce = Right-click on a Zotero item, and the following functions will appear in the context menu.
stylepersonal-tab-info-menu-title = Context Menu Features
stylepersonal-tab-info-menu-desc = Extra items in the right-click context menu: menu visibility manager, related items, AI tag generation, and AI remark generation.

stylepersonal-reader-functions = Reader
stylepersonal-reader-functions-introduce = When opening a PDF for reading, you can use the following functions.
stylepersonal-tab-info-reader-title = PDF Reading Enhancement
stylepersonal-tab-info-reader-desc = Features available when reading PDFs: background color, annotation color customization, merge annotations, and attachment version switching.

stylepersonal-tab-info-other-title = UI & System Settings
stylepersonal-tab-info-other-desc = Dark/light theme toggle, custom CSS injection, plus system settings for read time recording interval, repair, and startup delay.

stylepersonal-tab-info-storage-title = Reading Progress Storage
stylepersonal-tab-info-storage-desc = Reading progress is saved and synced across devices. Choose between Zotero Notes (recommended, auto-sync) or a local JSON file (custom path).
stylepersonal-Merge-Annotations =
    .label = Merge Annotations
    .tooltiptext = Some paragraphs span across pages. When highlighting such paragraphs, you need to mark them twice to get two annotations. Select these two annotations on the left side of the reading interface, right-click and click 'Merge Annotations' to delete second annotation, and add its information to the first annotation.
stylepersonal-Attachment-Version-Switch = 
    .label = Attachment Version Switch
    .tooltiptext = An Zotero item may contain multiple attachments. After opening an attachment, you can quickly switch to other attachments in the toolbar.
stylepersonal-Margin-Annotation = 
    .label = Margin Annotation
    .tooltiptext = Display annotations in the margins of the PDF.
stylepersonal-other-functions = Other
stylepersonal-storage-functions = Storage

stylepersonal-column-IF = 
    .label = Impact Factor Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the Impact Factor column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. This column requires configuring an easyscholar API key to display.
stylepersonal-Column-PublicationTags = 
    .label = Journal Tags Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the Journal Tags column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. This column requires configuring an easyscholar API key to display.

stylepersonal-column-Tags = 
    .label = Tags Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the Tags column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. Note that tags in Zotero can be assigned colors and positions. After assignment, they will appear as dots with the assigned color. These dot-style tags are originally displayed before the title. To display them there, open the title column settings and check "Tags."
stylepersonal-column-Creator = 
    .label = Creator Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, Zotero’s original Creator column will support displaying specific authors. You can configure this in the column settings.
stylepersonal-Column-Title = 
    .label = Title Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, Zotero’s original Title column will gain additional functionality. The reading progress of the literature will be visually displayed directly in the title. You can control whether to show tags, customize the reading progress color, or display translated titles in its column settings. By default, reading progress is stored in the notes section under Addon Item entries in the library. However, for data stability, it is recommended to switch to JSON storage as soon as possible.

stylepersonal-Translate-Shortcut = Toggle Translation Shortcut:
stylepersonal-Column-TextTags = 
    .label = #Tags
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the #Tags column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. Unlike regular tags, #Tags display the tag text instead of dots. Simply create tags starting with '#', and nesting is supported (e.g., '#1/2/3').
stylepersonal-Column-Status = 
    .label = Status Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the Status column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. This column allows quick switching of status tags for literature. Refolio specifies that status tags should start with '/'. For example, '/reading'. After creating a status tag, assign a color to it so it becomes a valid status tag. To switch statuses, click the rectangular area where the status tag should appear, and select from the available options.
stylepersonal-Column-Rating = 
    .label = Rating Column
    .tooltiptext = Quickly rate items with customizable symbols. Ratings are stored in the Extra field by default, or can be stored as star tags.
stylepersonal-rating-storage-location = Storage location
stylepersonal-rating-storage-extra =
    .label = Extra field
stylepersonal-rating-storage-tag =
    .label = As tag
stylepersonal-Column-Remark = 
    .label = Remark Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, the Remark column will appear in the entry panel of the main interface. You may have noticed the limitations of tags, even #Tags, which display limited text. The Remark column addresses this by allowing you to add a brief evaluation of the literature directly in the entry panel. You can edit remarks in the sidebar or use AI to generate remarks based on abstracts. Steps: Select multiple entries, right-click > AI Generate Remarks, and wait.
stylepersonal-Column-Publication = 
    .label = Publication Column
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, Zotero’s original Publication column will gain additional functionality. In its column settings, you can specify alternative fields to populate when the publication field is empty. For example, theses don’t have publications but include university information. After configuring 'university' as a fallback, this column will display the university for theses.
stylepersonal-Nested-Tags = 
    .label = Nested Tags View
    .tooltiptext = Refolio introduces the concept of #Tags and takes it further with nested tags. When you create a tag like '#1/2/3', it becomes a standard nested tag. But how do you visualize it? Zotero’s lower-left corner shows tags but doesn’t support nested tags. This function extends the tag display area to properly show nested tags.
stylepersonal-View-Manager = 
    .label = View Groups
    .tooltiptext = Refolio brings more possibilities to Zotero, supporting the display of additional columns. However, screen space is limited, making it hard to show all desired columns. This function helps quickly show/hide certain columns to meet various use cases. For example, when searching for papers, I usually show Title + Tags + Remark + Impact Factor (called View 1). While writing a paper, I show Title + #Tags + Rating (called View 2). Manually switching between views is cumbersome, but this function simplifies it. First, adjust the entry panel to View 1, then right-click any column name, scroll to the end, click View Groups > Add New View, enter a name, and save. Repeat for View 2. Created views will appear at the bottom of the column menu for quick switching.
stylepersonal-Dark-Light-Button = 
    .label = Light/Dark Theme Toggle Button
    .tooltiptext = On the top-left corner of Zotero, a sun/moon icon allows quick theme switching.
stylepersonal-Collection-Item-Count = 
    .label = Number of Items in Collection
    .tooltiptext = Displays the number of items in a collection next to the collection name in the left collection panel.
stylepersonal-Sort-Collection-Item =
    .label = Sort Collections
    .tooltiptext = Displays a sort button above the left collection panel.
stylepersonal-Favorite-Collections = 
    .label = Pin Collections
    .tooltiptext = Pins a collection in the left collection panel to the top, similar to favoriting a collection.
stylepersonal-Column-Read-Time = 
    .label = Reading Time Column
    .tooltiptext = A supplementary visualization of title reading progress, showing total reading time.
stylepersonal-PDF-Styles = 
    .label = PDF Background Color
    .tooltiptext = Once enabled, a PDF icon will appear in the reader toolbar, allowing adjustment of PDF background colors (this function will be natively supported by Zotero).
stylepersonal-Graph-View = 
    .label = Relationship Graph
    .tooltiptext = A Refolio plugin icon will appear in the toolbar of Zotero’s entry panel. Clicking it will display the relationship graph interface. Note: Move your mouse to the bottom-center of the relationship graph interface to reveal the red-dot toggle button.
stylepersonal-Add-Tags = 
    .label = Quick Add Tags
    .tooltiptext = Press the shortcut key in different states to bring up the tag addition panel, where you can select existing tags and add them to target entries. Target entries could be notes, attachment entries, annotations, or regular entries.
stylepersonal-Shortcut = Shortcut:

stylepersonal-Menu-Visibility-Manager =
    .label = Hide Right-Click Menu Items
    .tooltiptext = Enable the menu manager to hide or reorder items in the right-click context menu.

stylepersonal-Related-Items =
    .label = Related Items
    .tooltiptext = Select multiple entries, right-click > Link/Unlink Related Items.

stylepersonal-Column-Annotation = 
    .label = Annotation Column
    .tooltiptext = Directly displays the distribution status of annotations in the entry panel of the main interface. If performance lags, consider disabling this function.

stylepersonal-Use-Styles-from-Editor = 
    .label = Inject Custom CSS Styles into Zotero


